okay, a certain amount of skill is required to play nethack. you have to
be able to intentionally hit a given key on a keyboard when you are
ready. this isn't a real-time problem. actually, it isn't a skill
question at all, is it? my young nephew (i won't mention his age) enjoys
the game, seems to be able to move around where he wants, etc. and
usually dies because he's just not a very sophisticated player. his
"skills" aren't helping or hurting him but his lack of experience and
strategy clearly is. i did not intend this example to make any unwarranted
tangential implications. the point is i don't see "skill" as a real
issue. patience, deliberation, carefulness are issues ...

now about explore-mode, i didn't explain that carefully so i'll make a
second attempt, here. explore-mode (a way to play without playing the
one real game) should be configurable as needed to get the player upto
speed. i suggested that "not HARD" be a pre-game option. other options
would be (for example) "ask_create" and "confirm_boo_boos", etc. the
default explore-mode (i.e. with no options) should be, as greg suggested,
the _same_ as the real game (except that you should still get that
wand of wishing) with only the "Really Die? option remaining. if you can
explore at that level then you are ready for _the_ game. this is very
fair, and extremely generous, in my opinion.

